I had to take into consideration how i was going to implement the 3 inputs into x86. I used the
.bss section to hold values that the user inputs. I used d1 and d2 to hold the first two int values
and d3 to hold the final result for each interation of the loop. The loop uses the rcx register as a counter
to control iterations. The counter is decremented each cycle and jnz is used to repeat the loop
until the counter reaches zero. I took into consideration how to implement
the loop in x86 by using a register-based counter to control the number of iterations. 
I implemented Error handling by checking the return value of scanf. If the input was not successfully read, 
the program branches to an error handler which will display an error message and restarts the loop.

